---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";

// This page is the URL printed on the back of every card, so its path must
// stay /print. Content mirrors docs/printing.md.
import manifest from "../data/cards.json";

const DECK = [
  {
    href: "/cards/deck-a4-fold.pdf",
    name: "A4 — the whole set, one sheet",
    note: "Start here. Single-sided, fold, glue, cut. No duplex printer needed.",
  },
  {
    href: "/cards/deck-letter-fold.pdf",
    name: "US Letter — the whole set",
    note: "Same, Letter paper.",
  },
];

const DUPLEX = [
  {
    href: "/cards/deck-a4-duplex-long.pdf",
    name: "A4 two-sided, flip on LONG edge",
    note: "Two complete sets per sheet. Pick the file that matches your printer setting.",
  },
  {
    href: "/cards/deck-a4-duplex-short.pdf",
    name: "A4 two-sided, flip on SHORT edge",
    note: "Same sheet, laid out for the other flip.",
  },
  { href: "/cards/deck-letter-duplex-long.pdf", name: "US Letter, LONG edge", note: "" },
  { href: "/cards/deck-letter-duplex-short.pdf", name: "US Letter, SHORT edge", note: "" },
];

const VIEWERS = [
  ["Acrobat / Reader", "Page Sizing & Handling → Size → Actual size. Turn off “Auto portrait/landscape”."],
  ["macOS Preview", "Scale: 100 % radio button (not “Scale to Fit”). Pick A4 / US Letter, not the “borderless” variant."],
  ["Windows / Edge", "Page Sizing → Actual size."],
  ["Chrome", "More settings → Scale → Custom → 100. Its “Default” silently shrinks. Prefer another viewer."],
];
---

<Base
  title="Print the cards — Cubepath"
  description="Print the Cubepath card set at home: one fold-over sheet for all four cards, per-card reprints, and the settings that keep them wallet-sized."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <h1>Print the cards</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Four cards: three numbered progression cards and one annex. Each one leaves you
      able to solve a cube, and each says on its own back what unlocks the next.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Print the set</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        {
          DECK.map((f) => (
            <li>
              <a href={f.href}>{f.name}</a>
              <span>{f.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <details>
        <summary>Two-sided instead? Pick the file that matches your flip setting.</summary>
        <ul class="files">
          {
            DUPLEX.map((f) => (
              <li>
                <a href={f.href}>{f.name}</a>
                <span>{f.note}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="note">
          There is deliberately no single file that works under either flip. The numeral
          on both faces is your check — cut one card first and make sure its front and
          back agree.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Or reprint one card</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        {
          manifest.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={c.route}>
                {c.num ? `${c.num}/3` : "A"} — {c.title}
              </a>
              <span>
                <a href={`/cards/${c.fold_pdf.a4}`}>A4</a> ·{" "}
                <a href={`/cards/${c.fold_pdf.letter}`}>Letter</a> ·{" "}
                <a href={`/cards/${c.card_pdf}`}>bare card</a> — four copies per sheet.
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Print at 100 %</h2>
      <p>
        This is the one setting that matters. Never “Fit to page”, “Shrink oversized
        pages”, or “Scale to fit”. Each sheet carries an <strong>80 mm calibration bar</strong>
        in both margins — measure it after the first page. If it isn’t 80 mm, the scale is
        wrong and the card won’t fit a wallet slot.
      </p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {
            VIEWERS.map(([app, how]) => (
              <tr>
                <th>{app}</th>
                <td>{how}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">
        Check your printer driver’s own dialog too — a driver-level “Fit to Paper Size”
        overrides whatever the application asked for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Folding and two-sided</h2>
      <p>
        The default files are <strong>single-sided</strong>: print, crease the grey line,
        fold so both printed faces are outward, glue, then cut both layers together. That
        removes duplex registration error entirely, and works on printers with no duplex
        unit at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you do want two-sided, the set ships one file per flip direction. Each card
        carries its number on <em>both</em> faces, so a wrong flip is caught after cutting
        one card instead of after wasting the sheet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Paper and finishing</h2>
      <p>
        160–200 gsm feeds through most home printers. Cut on the grey hairlines — they run
        the full sheet, so one straight cut serves four cards.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        A standard 54 × 86 mm “credit card” laminating pouch leaves about 0.4 mm of total
        clearance and will not seal. Either keep it wallet-sized and don’t laminate (the
        folded 200 gsm card is stiff enough), or use a 60 × 90 mm business-card pouch and
        accept that the result no longer fits a wallet slot.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="lead">
      Also on paper: <a href="/cubepath.pdf">the full PDF guide</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 34px 20px 60px;
  }
  .lead {
    color: var(--soft);
    margin: 8px 0 10px;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  p {
    margin: 8px 0;
  }
  .note {
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .files {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .files li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 10px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .files a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .files span {
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 10px 0;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 8px 10px 8px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  th {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--soft);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
